(33, 'a', '\nAbhorrent', ' adj. (often foll. By to) disgusting or hateful.'),
(34, 'a', '\nAbide', ' v. (-ding; past abided or rarely abode) 1 (usu. In neg.) Tolerate, endure (can''t abide him). 2 (foll. By by) a act in accordance with (abide by the rules). B keep (a promise). 3 archaic remain, continue. [old english a- intensive prefix, *bide]'),
(35, 'a', '\nAbiding', ' adj. Enduring, permanent.'),
