(60, 'a', '\nAbominable', ' adj. 1 detestable, loathsome. 2 colloq. Very unpleasant (abominable weather).  abominably adv. [latin abominor deprecate]'),
(61, 'a', '\nAbominable', 'snowman  n. Supposed manlike or bearlike himalayan animal; yeti.'),
(62, 'a', '\nAbominate', ' v. (-ting) detest, loathe.  abomination n. [latin: related to *abominable]'),
(63, 'a', '\nAboriginal', ' â€”adj. 1 indigenous, inhabiting a land from the earliest times, esp. Before the arrival of colonists. 2 (usu. Aboriginal) of australian aborigines. â€”n. 1 aboriginal inhabitant. 2 (usu. Aboriginal) aboriginal inhabitant of australia. [latin: related to *origin]'),
(64, 'a', '\nAborigine', ' n. (usu. In pl.) 1 aboriginal inhabitant. 2 (usu. Aborigine) aboriginal inhabitant of australia.'),
(65, 'a', '\nUsage', ' when referring to the people, aboriginal is preferred for the singular form and aborigines for the plural, although aboriginals is also acceptable.'),
(66, 'a', '\nAbort', ' v. 1 miscarry. 2 a effect abortion of (a foetus). B effect abortion in (a mother). 3 end or cause (a project etc.) To end before completion. [latin orior be born]'),
(67, 'a', '\nAbortion', ' n. 1 natural or (esp.) Induced expulsion of a foetus from the womb before it is able to survive independently. 2 stunted or deformed creature or thing. 3 failed project or action.  abortionist n.'),
