(69, 'a', '\nAborigine', ' n. (usu. In pl.) 1 aboriginal inhabitant. 2 (usu. Aborigine) aboriginal inhabitant of australia.'),
(70, 'a', '\nUsage', ' when referring to the people, aboriginal is preferred for the singular form and aborigines for the plural, although aboriginals is also acceptable.'),
(71, 'a', '\nAbort', ' v. 1 miscarry. 2 a effect abortion of (a foetus). B effect abortion in (a mother). 3 end or cause (a project etc.) To end before completion. [latin orior be born]'),
