(90, 'a', '\nAbseil', ' â€”v. Descend by using a doubled rope coiled round the body and fixed at a higher point. â€”n. Descent made by abseiling. [german ab down, seil rope]'),
(91, 'a', '\nAbsence', ' n. 1 being away. 2 time of this. 3 (foll. By of) lack of.  absence of mind inattentiveness. [latin absentia]'),
