(788, 'a', '\nAlly', ' â€”n. (pl. -ies) state, person, etc., formally cooperating or united with another, esp. (also ally) in war. â€”v. Also (-ies, -ied) (often refl. And foll. By with) combine in alliance. [latin alligo bind]'),
