(1523, 'a', '\nAristocracy', ' n. (pl. -ies) 1 ruling class or Ã©lite; nobility. 2 a government by an Ã©lite. B state so governed. 3 (often foll. By of) best representatives. [greek aristokratia rule by the best]'),
