(1560, 'a', '\nArose', ' past of *arise.'),
(1561, 'a', '\nAround', ' â€”adv. 1 on every side; all round; round about. 2 colloq. A in existence; available. B near at hand. 3 here and there (shop around). â€”prep. 1 on or along the circuit of. 2 on every side of. 3 here and there in or near (chairs around the room). 4 a round (church around the corner). B at a time near to (came around four o''clock).  have been around colloq. Be widely experienced.'),
