(1599, 'a', '\nArthropod', ' n. Invertebrate with a segmented body and jointed limbs, e.g. An insect, spider, or crustacean. [greek arthron joint, pous pod- foot]'),
(1600, 'a', '\nArthropod', ' n. Invertebrate with a segmented body and jointed limbs, e.g. An insect, spider, or crustacean. [greek arthron joint, pous pod- foot]'),
(1601, 'a', '\nArtichoke', ' n. 1 plant allied to the thistle. 2 (in full globe artichoke) its partly edible flower-head (see also *jerusalem artichoke). [italian from arabic]'),
(1602, 'a', '\nArticle', ' â€”n. 1 item or thing. 2 non-fictional journalistic essay. 3 clause or item in an agreement or contract. 4 definite or indefinite article. â€”v. (-ling) employ under contract as a trainee. [latin articulus from artus joint]'),
