(1626, 'a', '\nAryan', ' â€”n. 1 speaker of any of the languages of the indo-european family. 2 improperly (in nazi ideology) non-jewish caucasian. â€”adj. Of aryans. [sanskrit]'),
(1627, 'a', '\nAs', ' symb. Arsenic.'),
(1628, 'a', '\nAs1', ' â€”adv. & conj. (adv. As antecedent in main sentence; conj. In relative clause expressed or implied) to the extent to which â€¦ is or does etc. (am as tall as he; am as tall as he is; (colloq.) Am as tall as him; as recently as last week). â€”conj. (with relative clause expressed or implied) 1 (with antecedent so) expressing result or purpose (came early so as to meet us). 2 (with antecedent adverb omitted) although (good as it is = although it is good). 3 (without antecedent adverb) a in the manner in which (do as you like; rose as one man). B in the capacity or form of (i speak as your friend; olivier as hamlet). C while (arrived as i was eating). D since, seeing that (as you are here, we can talk). E for instance (cathedral cities, as york). â€”rel. Pron.'),
(1629, 'a', '\nAs2', ' n. (pl. Asses) roman copper coin. [latin]'),
