(2648, 'b', '\r\nBiro', ' n. (pl. -s) propr. A kind of ball-point pen. [birÃ³, name of its inventor]'),
(2649, 'b', '\r\nBirth', ' n. 1 emergence of a baby or young from its mother''s body. 2 beginning (birth of civilization). 3 a ancestry (of noble birth). B high or noble birth; inherited position.  give birth to 1 produce (young). 2 be the cause of. [old norse]'),
