(2672, 'b', '\r\nBit1', ' n. 1 small piece or quantity. 2 (prec. By a) fair amount (sold quite a bit). 3 often colloq. Short or small time, distance, or amount (wait a bit; move up a bit; a bit tired; a bit of an idiot).  bit by bit gradually. Do one''s bit colloq. Make a useful contribution. [old english]'),
