(2729, 'b', '\r\nBlackmail', ' â€”n. 1 a extortion of payment in return for silence. B payment so extorted. 2 use of threats or moral pressure. â€”v. 1 (try to) extort money etc. From by blackmail. 2 threaten, coerce.  blackmailer n. [obsolete mail rent]'),
