(3286, 'b', '\r\nBrake1', ' â€”n. 1 (often in pl.) Device for stopping or slowing a wheel, vehicle, etc. 2 thing that impedes. â€”v. (-king) 1 apply a brake. 2 slow or stop with a brake. [probably obsolete brake = curb]'),
(3287, 'b', '\r\nBrake2', ' n. Large estate car. [var. Of *break]'),
(3288, 'b', '\r\nBrake3', ' â€”n. 1 toothed instrument for crushing flax and hemp. 2 (in full brake harrow) heavy harrow. â€”v. (-king)  crush (flax or hemp). [low german or dutch: related to *break]'),
