(3317, 'b', '\r\nBrave', ' â€”adj. 1 able or ready to face and endure danger, disgrace, or pain. 2 formal splendid, spectacular. â€”n. American indian warrior. â€”v. (-ving) face bravely or defiantly.  bravely adv. Braveness n. Bravery n. [ultimately latin barbarus barbarian]'),
