(3327, 'b', '\r\nBrazil', ' n. 1 tall s. American tree. 2 (in full brazil nut) its large three-sided nut. [brazil in s. America]'),
(3328, 'b', '\r\nBreach', ' â€”n. 1 (often foll. By of) breaking or non-observation of a law, contract, etc. 2 breaking of relations; quarrel. 3 opening, gap. â€”v. 1 break through; make a gap in. 2 break (a law, contract, etc.).  step into the breach help in a crisis, esp. As a replacement. [germanic: related to *break]'),
