(6983, 'c', '\r\nCable', ' â€”n. 1 encased group of insulated wires for transmitting electricity etc. 2 thick rope of wire or hemp. 3 cablegram. 4 (in full cable stitch) knitting stitch resembling twisted rope. â€”v. (-ling) transmit (a message) or inform (a person) by cablegram. [latin caplum halter, from arabic]'),
