(7024, 'c', '\r\nCaftan', ' n. (also kaftan) 1 long tunic worn by men in the near east. 2 long loose dress or shirt. [turkish]'),
(7025, 'c', '\r\nCage', ' â€”n. 1 structure of bars or wires, esp. For confining animals or birds. 2 similar open framework, esp. A lift in mine etc. â€”v. (-ging) place or keep in a cage. [latin cavea]'),
