(7048, 'c', '\r\nCalciferous', ' adj. Yielding calcium salts, esp. Calcium carbonate.'),
(7049, 'c', '\r\nCalcify', ' v. (-ies, -ied) 1 harden by the depositing of calcium salts. 2 convert or be converted to calcium carbonate.  calcification n.'),
(7050, 'c', '\r\nCalcine', ' v. (-ning) decompose or be decomposed by strong heat.  calcination n. [french or medieval latin: related to *calx]'),
