(7422, 'c', '\r\nCarpel', ' n. Female reproductive organ of a flower. [greek karpos fruit]'),
(7423, 'c', '\r\nCarpenter', ' â€”n. Person skilled in woodwork. â€”v. 1 make or construct in wood. 2 construct; fit together.  carpentry n. [latin carpentum wagon]'),
(7424, 'c', '\r\nCarpet', ' â€”n. 1 a thick fabric for covering floor or stairs. B piece of this. 2 thing resembling this etc. (carpet of snow). â€”v. (-t-) 1 cover with or as with carpet. 2 colloq. Reprimand.  on the carpet colloq. 1 being reprimanded. 2 under consideration. Sweep under the carpet conceal (a problem or difficulty). [latin carpo pluck]'),
(7425, 'c', '\r\nCarpet-bag', ' n. Travelling-bag, orig. Made of carpet-like material.'),
