(7620, 'c', '\r\nCaucasoid', ' adj. Of caucasians.'),
(7621, 'c', '\r\nCaucus', ' n. (pl. -es) 1 us meeting of party members, esp. In the senate etc., to decide policy. 2 often derog. A meeting of a group within a larger organization or party. B such a group. [perhaps from algonquian]'),
