(7640, 'c', '\r\nCauterize', ' v. (also -ise) (-zing or -sing) burn (tissue), esp. To stop bleeding. [french: related to *caustic]'),
(7641, 'c', '\r\nCaution', ' â€”n. 1 attention to safety; prudence, carefulness. 2 a law warning, esp. A formal one. B warning and reprimand. 3 colloq. Amusing or surprising person or thing. â€”v. 1 warn or admonish. 2 issue a caution to. [latin caveo take heed]'),
