(7647, 'c', '\r\nCave', ' â€”n. Large hollow in the side of a cliff, hill, etc., or underground. â€”v. (-ving) explore caves.  cave in 1 (cause to) subside or collapse. 2 yield, give up. [latin cavus hollow]'),
