(7676, 'c', '\r\nCecum', ' n. (brit. Caecum) (pl. -ca) blind-ended pouch at the junction of the small and large intestines. [latin caecus blind]'),
(7677, 'c', '\r\nCedar', ' n. 1 spreading evergreen conifer. 2 its hard fragrant wood. [greek kedros]'),
(7678, 'c', '\r\nCede', ' v. (-ding) formal give up one''s rights to or possession of. [latin cedo cess- yield]'),
(7679, 'c', '\r\nCedilla', ' n. 1 mark written under c, esp. In french, to show it is sibilant (as in faÃ§ade). 2 similar mark under s in turkish etc. [spanish diminutive of zeda z]'),
