(7684, 'c', '\r\nCelebrant', ' n. Person who performs a rite, esp. The priest at the eucharist.'),
(7685, 'c', '\r\nCelebrate', ' v. (-ting) 1 mark with or engage in festivities. 2 perform (a rite or ceremony). 3 praise publicly.  celebration n. Celebrator n. Celebratory adj. [latin celeber renowned]'),
