(8566, 'c', '\r\nCoarse', ' adj. 1 rough or loose in texture; made of large particles. 2 lacking refinement; crude, obscene.  coarsely adv. Coarseness n. [origin unknown]'),
(8567, 'c', '\r\nCoarse', 'fish  n. Freshwater fish other than salmon and trout.'),
(8568, 'c', '\r\nCoarsen', ' v. Make or become coarse.'),
(8569, 'c', '\r\nCoast', ' â€”n. Border of land near the sea; seashore. â€”v. 1 ride or move, usu. Downhill, without the use of power. 2 make progress without much effort. 3 sail along the coast.  the coast is clear there is no danger of being observed or caught.  coastal adj. [latin costa side]'),
