(8609, 'c', '\r\nCockney', ' â€”n. (pl. -s) 1 native of london, esp. Of the east end. 2 dialect or accent used there. â€”adj. Of cockneys or their dialect. [cokeney â€˜cock''s eggâ€™]'),
(8610, 'c', '\r\nCockpit', ' n. 1 a compartment for the pilot (and crew) of an aircraft or spacecraft. B driver''s seat in a racing car. C space for the helmsman in some yachts. 2 arena of war or other conflict. 3 place for cock-fights.'),
