(9072, 'c', '\r\nConcentration', 'camp  n. Camp where political prisoners etc. Are detained.'),
(9073, 'c', '\r\nConcentric', ' adj. Having a common centre.  concentrically adv. [french or medieval latin: related to *centre]'),
(9074, 'c', '\r\nConcept', ' n. General notion; abstract idea. [latin: related to *conceive]'),
(9075, 'c', '\r\nConception', ' n. 1 conceiving or being conceived. 2 idea, plan. 3 understanding (has no conception). conceptional adj. [french from latin: related to *concept]'),
(9076, 'c', '\r\nConceptual', ' adj. Of mental conceptions or concepts.  conceptually adv.'),
(9077, 'c', '\r\nConceptualize', ' v. (also -ise) (-zing or -sing) form a concept or idea of.  conceptualization n.'),
(9078, 'c', '\r\nConcern', ' â€”v. 1 a be relevant or important to. B relate to; be about. 2 (refl.; often foll. By with, about, in) interest or involve oneself. 3 worry, affect. â€”n. 1 anxiety, worry. 2 a matter of interest or importance to one. B interest, connection (has a concern in politics). 3 business, firm. 4 colloq. Complicated thing, contrivance. [latin cerno sift]'),
(9079, 'c', '\r\nConcerned', ' adj. 1 involved, interested. 2 troubled, anxious.  be concerned (often foll. By in) take part.  concernedly adv. Concernedness n.'),
(9080, 'c', '\r\nConcerning', ' prep. About, regarding.'),
(9081, 'c', '\r\nConcert', ' n. 1 musical performance of usu. Several separate compositions. 2 agreement. 3 combination of voices or sounds. [italian: related to *concerto]'),
(9082, 'c', '\r\nConcerted', ' adj. 1 jointly arranged or planned. 2 mus. Arranged in parts for voices or instruments.'),
(9083, 'c', '\r\nConcertina', ' â€”n. Musical instrument like an accordion but smaller. â€”v. (-nas, -naed or -na''d, -naing) compress or collapse in folds like those of a concertina.'),
(9084, 'c', '\r\nConcerto', ' n. (pl. -s or -ti) composition for solo instrument(s) and orchestra. [italian]'),
(9085, 'c', '\r\nConcert', 'pitch  n. Pitch internationally agreed whereby the a above middle c = 440 hz.'),
(9086, 'c', '\r\nConcession', ' n. 1 a conceding. B thing conceded. 2 reduction in price for a certain category of persons. 3 a right to use land etc. B right to sell goods in a particular territory.  concessionary adj. [latin: related to *concede]'),
