(9097, 'c', '\r\nConcoct', ' v. 1 make by mixing ingredients. 2 invent (a story, lie, etc.).  concoction n. [latin coquo coct- cook]'),
(9098, 'c', '\r\nConcomitant', ' â€”adj. (often foll. By with) accompanying; occurring together. â€”n. Accompanying thing.  concomitance n. [latin comes comit- companion]'),
