(9181, 'c', '\r\nConfound', ' â€”v. 1 perplex, baffle. 2 confuse (in one''s mind). 3 archaic defeat, overthrow. â€”int. Expressing annoyance (confound you!). [latin confundo -fus- mix up]'),
