(9863, 'c', '\r\nCramp', ' â€”n. 1 painful involuntary muscular contraction. 2 (also cramp-iron) metal bar with bent ends for holding masonry etc. Together. â€”v. 1 affect with cramp. 2 (often foll. By up) confine narrowly. 3 restrict. 4 fasten with a cramp.  cramp a person''s style prevent a person from acting freely or naturally. [low german or dutch]'),
(9864, 'c', '\r\nCramped', ' adj. 1 (of a space) too small. 2 (of handwriting) small and with the letters close together.'),
