(9892, 'c', '\r\nCrater', ' â€”n. 1 mouth of a volcano. 2 bowl-shaped cavity, esp. That made by a shell or bomb. 3 hollow on the surface of a planet or moon, caused by impact. â€”v. Form a crater in. [greek, = mixing-bowl]'),
