(14070, 'e', '\r\nElucidate', ' v. (-ting) throw light on; explain.  elucidation n. Elucidatory adj. [latin: related to *lucid]'),
(14071, 'e', '\r\nElude', ' v. (-ding) 1 escape adroitly from (danger, pursuit, etc.). 2 avoid compliance with (a law etc.) Or fulfilment of (an obligation). 3 baffle (a person or memory etc.).  elusion n. [latin ludo play]'),
(14072, 'e', '\r\nElusive', ' adj. 1 difficult to find or catch. 2 difficult to remember. 3 avoiding the point raised.  elusiveness n.'),
