(14081, 'e', '\r\nEmail', ' n. (also e-mail) = *electronic mail.'),
(14082, 'e', '\r\nEmanate', ' v. (-ting) (usu. Foll. By from) issue or originate (from a source).  emanation n. [latin mano flow]'),
(14083, 'e', '\r\nEmancipate', ' v. (-ting) 1 free from social or political restraint. 2 (usu. As emancipated adj.) Free from the inhibitions of moral or social conventions. 3 free from slavery.  emancipation n. Emancipatory adj. [latin, = free from possession, from manus hand, capio take]'),
(14084, 'e', '\r\nEmasculate', ' â€”v. (-ting) 1 deprive of force or vigour. 2 castrate. â€”adj. 1 deprived of force. 2 castrated. 3 effeminate.  emasculation n. [latin: related to *male]'),
