(14106, 'e', '\r\nEmbrace', ' â€”v. (-cing) 1 a hold closely in the arms. B (absol., of two people) embrace each other. 2 clasp, enclose. 3 accept eagerly (an offer etc.). 4 adopt (a cause, idea, etc.). 5 include, comprise. 6 take in with the eye or mind. â€”n. Act of embracing, clasp.  embraceable adj. [latin: related to *brace]'),
