(14118, 'e', '\r\nEmerald', 'isle  n. Ireland.'),
(14119, 'e', '\r\nEmerge', ' v. (-ging) 1 come up or out into view. 2 (of facts etc.) Become known, be revealed. 3 become recognized or prominent. 4 (of a question, difficulty, etc.) Become apparent.  emergence n. Emergent adj. [latin: related to *merge]'),
(14120, 'e', '\r\nEmergency', ' n. (pl. -ies) 1 sudden state of danger etc., requiring immediate action. 2 a condition requiring immediate treatment. B patient with this. 3 (attrib.) For use in an emergency. [medieval latin: related to *emerge]'),
