(14383, 'e', '\r\nEpitaph', ' n. Words written in memory of a dead person, esp. As a tomb inscription. [greek taphos tomb]'),
(14384, 'e', '\r\nEpithelium', ' n. (pl. -s or -lia) tissue forming the outer layer of the body and lining many hollow structures.  epithelial adj. [greek thele teat]'),
