(14386, 'e', '\r\nEpitome', ' n. 1 person or thing embodying a quality etc. 2 thing representing another in miniature. [greek temno cut]'),
(14387, 'e', '\r\nEpitomize', ' v. (also -ise) (-zing or -sing) make or be a perfect example of (a quality etc.).'),
(14388, 'e', '\r\nEpns', ' abbr. Electroplated nickel silver.'),
(14389, 'e', '\r\nEpoch', ' n. 1 period of history etc. Marked by notable events. 2 beginning of an era. 3 geol. Division of a period, corresponding to a set of strata.  epochal adj. [greek, = pause]'),
