(14478, 'e', '\r\nErbium', ' n. Metallic element of the lanthanide series. [ytterby in sweden]'),
(14479, 'e', '\r\nEre', ' prep. & conj. Poet. Or archaic before (of time) (ere noon; ere they come). [old english]'),
(14480, 'e', '\r\nErect', ' â€”adj. 1 upright, vertical. 2 (of the penis etc.) Enlarged and rigid, esp. In sexual excitement. 3 (of hair) bristling. â€”v. 1 set up; build. 2 establish.  erection n. Erectly adv. Erectness n. [latin erigere erect- set up]'),
