(14664, 'e', '\r\nEt', 'al.  Abbr. And others. [latin et alii]'),
(14665, 'e', '\r\nEtc.', ' Abbr. = *et cetera.'),
(14666, 'e', '\r\nEt', 'cetera  (also etcetera) â€”adv. 1 and the rest. 2 and so on. â€”n. (in pl.) The usual extras. [latin]'),
(14667, 'e', '\r\nEtch', ' v. 1 a reproduce (a picture etc.) By engraving it on a metal plate with acid (esp. To print copies). B engrave (a plate) in this way. 2 practise this craft. 3 (foll. By on, upon) impress deeply (esp. On the mind).  etcher n. [dutch etsen]'),
