(14955, 'e', '\r\nExpound', ' v. 1 set out in detail. 2 explain or interpret. [latin pono posit- place]'),
(14956, 'e', '\r\nExpress', ' â€”v. 1 represent or make known in words or by gestures, conduct, etc. 2 refl. Communicate what one thinks, feels, or means. 3 esp. Math. Represent by symbols. 4 squeeze out (liquid or air). 5 send by express service. â€”adj. 1 operating at high speed. 2 also definitely stated. 3 delivered by a specially fast service. â€”adv. 1 at high speed. 2 by express messenger or train. â€”n. 1 express train etc. 2 us service for the rapid transport of parcels etc.  expressible adj. Expressly adv. (in sense 2 of adj.). [latin exprimo -press- squeeze out]'),
(14957, 'e', '\r\nExpression', ' n. 1 expressing or being expressed. 2 word or phrase expressed. 3 person''s facial appearance, indicating feeling. 4 conveying of feeling in music, speaking, dance, etc. 5 depiction of feeling etc. In art. 6 math. Collection of symbols expressing a quantity.  expressionless adj. [french: related to *express]'),
(14958, 'e', '\r\nExpressionism', ' n. Style of painting, music, drama, etc., seeking to express emotion rather than the external world.  expressionist n. & adj.'),
(14959, 'e', '\r\nExpressive', ' adj. 1 full of expression (expressive look). 2 (foll. By of) serving to express.  expressively adv. Expressiveness n.'),
(14960, 'e', '\r\nExpresso', ' var. Of *espresso.'),
(14961, 'e', '\r\nExpressway', ' n. Us motorway.'),
(14962, 'e', '\r\nExpropriate', ' v. (-ting) 1 take away (property) from its owner. 2 (foll. By from) dispossess.  expropriation n. Expropriator n. [latin proprium property]'),
