(15004, 'f', '\r\nFact', 'of life  n. Something that must be accepted.'),
(15005, 'f', '\r\nFactor', ' n. 1 circumstance etc. Contributing to a result. 2 whole number etc. That when multiplied with another produces a given number. 3 a business agent. B scot. Land-agent, steward. C agent, deputy. [latin: related to *fact]'),
