(15014, 'f', '\r\nFactual', ' adj. Based on or concerned with fact.  factually adv.'),
(15015, 'f', '\r\nFaculty', ' n. (pl. -ies) 1 aptitude for a particular activity. 2 inherent mental or physical power. 3 a group of related university departments. B us teaching staff of a university or college. 4 authorization, esp. By a church authority. [latin: related to *facile]'),
