(15099, 'f', '\r\nFamous', ' adj. 1 (often foll. By for) celebrated; well-known. 2 colloq. Excellent.  famously adv. [latin: related to *fame]'),
(15100, 'f', '\r\nFan1', ' â€”n. 1 apparatus, usu. With rotating blades, for ventilation etc. 2 folding semicircular device waved to cool oneself. 3 thing spread out like a fan (fan tracery). â€”v. (-nn-) 1 blow air on, with or as with a fan. 2 (of a breeze) blow gently on. 3 (usu. Foll. By out) spread out like a fan. [latin vannus winnowing-basket]'),
(15101, 'f', '\r\nFan2', ' n. Devotee of a particular activity, performer, etc. (film fan). [abbreviation of *fanatic]'),
(15102, 'f', '\r\nFanatic', ' â€”n. Person obsessively devoted to a belief, activity, etc. â€”adj. Excessively enthusiastic.  fanatical adj. Fanatically adv. Fanaticism n. [latin fanum temple]'),
(15103, 'f', '\r\nFan', 'belt  n. Belt driving a fan to cool the radiator in a vehicle.'),
