(15105, 'f', '\r\nFanciful', ' adj. 1 imaginary. 2 indulging in fancies.  fancifully adv.'),
(15106, 'f', '\r\nFan', 'club  n. Club of devotees.'),
(15107, 'f', '\r\nFancy', ' â€”n. (pl. -ies) 1 inclination. 2 whim. 3 supposition. 4 a faculty of imagination. B mental image. â€”adj. (-ier, -iest) 1 ornamental. 2 extravagant. â€”v. (-ies, -ied) 1 (foll. By that) be inclined to suppose. 2 colloq. Feel a desire for (fancy a drink?). 3 colloq. Find sexually attractive. 4 colloq. Value (oneself, one''s ability, etc.) Unduly highly. 5 (in imper.) Exclamation of surprise. 6 imagine.  take a fancy to become (esp. Inexplicably) fond of. Take a person''s fancy suddenly attract or please.  fanciable adj. (in sense 3 of v.). Fancily adv. Fanciness n. [contraction of *fantasy]'),
(15108, 'f', '\r\nFancy', 'dress  n. Costume for masquerading at a party.'),
(15109, 'f', '\r\nFancy-free', ' adj. Without (esp. Emotional) commitments.'),
