(15136, 'f', '\r\nFar', 'gone  adj. Colloq. Very ill, drunk, etc.'),
(15137, 'f', '\r\nFarina', ' n. 1 flour or meal of cereal, nuts, or starchy roots. 2 starch.  farinaceous adj. [latin]'),
(15138, 'f', '\r\nFarm', ' â€”n. 1 land and its buildings under one management for growing crops, rearing animals, etc. 2 such land etc. For a specified purpose (trout-farm). 3 = *farmhouse. â€”v. 1 a use (land) for growing crops, rearing animals, etc. B be a farmer; work on a farm. 2 breed (fish etc.) Commercially. 3 (often foll. By out) delegate or subcontract (work) to others.  farming n. [french ferme from latin firma fixed payment]'),
