(15159, 'f', '\r\nFasces', ' n.pl. 1 rom. Hist. Bundle of rods with a projecting axe-blade, as a magistrate''s symbol of power. 2 emblems of authority. [latin, pl. Of fascis bundle]'),
(15160, 'f', '\r\nFascia', ' n. (also facia) (pl. -s) 1 a instrument panel of a vehicle. B similar panel etc. For operating machinery. 2 strip with a name etc. Over a shop-front. 3 a long flat surface in classical architecture. B flat surface, usu. Of wood, covering the ends of rafters. 4 stripe or band. [latin, = band, door-frame]'),
