(15342, 'f', '\r\nFetch', ' â€”v. 1 go for and bring back (fetch a doctor). 2 be sold for (a price) (fetched Â£10). 3 cause (blood, tears, etc.) To flow. 4 draw (breath), heave (a sigh). 5 colloq. Give (a blow etc.) (fetched him a slap). â€”n.'),
