(15360, 'f', '\r\nFew', ' â€”adj. Not many (few doctors smoke). â€”n. (as pl.) 1 (prec. By a) some but not many (a few of his friends were there). 2 not many (few are chosen). 3 (prec. By the) a the minority. B the elect.  a good few colloq. Fairly large number. No fewer than as many as (a specified number). Not a few a considerable number. [old english]'),
(15361, 'f', '\r\nFew', 'and far between  predic. Adj. Scarce.'),
