(16212, 'f', '\r\nForte2', ' mus. â€”adj. Loud. â€”adv. Loudly. â€”n. Loud playing or passage. [italian: related to *fort]'),
(16213, 'f', '\r\nForth', ' adv. Archaic except in set phrases 1 forward; into view (bring forth; come forth). 2 onwards in time (from this time forth). 3 forwards (back and forth). 4 out from a starting-point (set forth).  and so forth see *so1. [old english]'),
