(16304, 'f', '\r\nFrank', ' â€”adj. 1 candid, outspoken. 2 undisguised. 3 open. â€”v. Mark (a letter) to record the payment of postage. â€”n. Franking signature or mark.  frankly adv. Frankness n. [latin francus free: related to *frank]'),
