(16427, 'f', '\r\nFriend', ' n. 1 person one likes and chooses to spend time with (usu. Without sexual or family bonds). 2 sympathizer, helper. 3 ally or neutral person (friend or foe?). 4 person already mentioned (our friend at the bank). 5 regular supporter of an institution. 6 (friend) quaker. [old english]'),
(16428, 'f', '\r\nFriendly', ' â€”adj. (-ier, -iest) 1 outgoing, well-disposed, kindly. 2 a (often foll. By with) on amicable terms. B not hostile. 3 (in comb.) Not harming; helping (ozone-friendly; user-friendly). 4 = *user-friendly. â€”n. (pl. -ies) = *friendly match. â€”adv. In a friendly manner.  friendliness n.'),
(16429, 'f', '\r\nFriendly', 'match  n. Match played for enjoyment rather than competition.'),
(16430, 'f', '\r\nFriendly', 'society  n. Insurance society insuring against illness etc.'),
