(16441, 'f', '\r\nFrill', ' â€”n. 1 strip of gathered or pleated material as an ornamental edging. 2 (in pl.) Unnecessary embellishments. â€”v. Decorate with a frill.  frilly adj. (-ier, -iest). [origin unknown]'),
(16442, 'f', '\r\nFringe', ' â€”n. 1 border of tassels or loose threads. 2 front hair hanging over the forehead. 3 outer limit of an area, population, etc. (often attrib.: fringe theatre). 4 unimportant area or part. â€”v. (-ging) 1 adorn with a fringe. 2 serve as a fringe to. [latin fimbria]'),
