(16509, 'f', '\r\nFrustum', ' n. (pl. -ta or -s) geom. Remaining part of a decapitated cone or pyramid. [latin, = piece cut off]'),
(16510, 'f', '\r\nFry1', ' â€”v. (fries, fried) cook or be cooked in hot fat. â€”n. (pl. Fries) 1 offal, usu. Eaten fried (lamb''s fry). 2 fried food, esp. Meat. [latin frigo]'),
(16511, 'f', '\r\nFry2', ' n.pl. Young or newly hatched fishes. [old norse, = seed]'),
