(16523, 'f', '\r\nFudge', ' â€”n. 1 soft toffee-like sweet made of milk, sugar, butter, etc. 2 piece of dishonesty or faking. â€”v. (-ging) make or do clumsily or dishonestly; fake (fudge the results). [origin uncertain]'),
(16524, 'f', '\r\nFuehrer', ' var. Of *fÃ¼hrer.'),
(16525, 'f', '\r\nFuel', ' â€”n. 1 material for burning or as a source of heat, power, or nuclear energy. 2 food as a source of energy. 3 thing that sustains or inflames passion etc. â€”v. (-ll-; us -l-) 1 supply with, take in, or get, fuel. 2 inflame (feeling etc.). [french from latin]'),
