(17186, 'g', '\r\nGlow', ' â€”v. 1 a emit light and heat without flame. B shine as if heated in this way.  2 (often foll. By with) a (of the body) be heated. B show or feel strong emotion (glowed with pride). 3 show a warm colour. 4 (as glowing adj.) Expressing pride or satisfaction (glowing report). â€”n. 1 glowing state. 2 bright warm colour. 3 feeling of satisfaction or well-being. [old english]'),
