(17265, 'g', '\r\nGo-getter', ' n. Colloq. Aggressively enterprising person.'),
(17266, 'g', '\r\nGoggle', ' â€”v. (-ling) 1 a (often foll. By at) look with wide-open eyes. B (of the eyes) be rolled about; protrude. 2 roll (the eyes). â€”adj. (usu. Attrib.) (of the eyes) protuberant or rolling. â€”n. (in pl.) Spectacles for protecting the eyes. [probably imitative]'),
