(17642, 'g', '\r\nGroan', ' â€”v. 1 a make a deep sound expressing pain, grief, or disapproval. B utter with groans. 2 (usu. Foll. By under, beneath, with) be loaded or oppressed. â€”n. Sound made in groaning. [old english]'),
(17643, 'g', '\r\nGroat', ' n. Hist. Silver coin worth four old pence. [low german or dutch: related to *great]'),
(17644, 'g', '\r\nGroats', ' n.pl. Hulled or crushed grain, esp. Oats. [old english]'),
(17645, 'g', '\r\nGrocer', ' n. Dealer in food and household provisions. [anglo-french grosser from latin grossus *gross]'),
