(17655, 'g', '\r\nGrope', ' â€”v. (-ping) 1 (usu. Foll. By for) feel about or search blindly. 2 (foll. By for, after) search mentally. 3 feel (one''s way) towards something. 4 slang fondle clumsily for sexual pleasure. â€”n. Act of groping. [old english]'),
(17656, 'g', '\r\nGrosgrain', ' n. Corded fabric of silk etc. [french, = coarse grain: related to *gross, *grain]'),
(17657, 'g', '\r\nGros', 'point  n. Cross-stitch embroidery on canvas. [french: related to *gross, *point]'),
(17658, 'g', '\r\nGross', ' â€”adj. 1 overfed, bloated. 2 (of a person, manners, or morals) coarse, unrefined, or indecent. 3 flagrant (gross negligence). 4 total; not net (gross tonnage). 5 (of the senses etc.) Dull. â€”v. Produce as gross profit. â€”n. (pl. Same) amount equal to twelve dozen.  grossly adv. Grossness n. [latin grossus]'),
