(17702, 'g', '\r\nGroyne', ' n. (us groin) timber, stone, or concrete wall built at right angles to the coast to check beach erosion. [dial. Groin snout, from french]'),
(17703, 'g', '\r\nGrub', ' â€”n. 1 larva of an insect. 2 colloq. Food. â€”v. (-bb-) 1 dig superficially. 2 (foll. By up, out) a extract by digging. B extract (information etc.) By searching in books etc. 3 rummage. [old english]'),
