(17708, 'g', '\r\nGruelling', ' adj. (us grueling) extremely demanding or tiring.'),
(17709, 'g', '\r\nGruesome', ' adj. Horrible, grisly, disgusting.  gruesomely adv. [scandinavian]'),
(17710, 'g', '\r\nGruff', ' adj. 1 a (of a voice) low and harsh. B (of a person) having a gruff voice. 2 surly.  gruffly adv. Gruffness n. [low german or dutch grof coarse]'),
