(17737, 'g', '\r\nGuess', ' â€”v. 1 (often absol.) Estimate without calculation or measurement. 2 form a hypothesis or opinion about; conjecture; think likely. 3 conjecture or estimate correctly. 4 (foll. By at) make a conjecture about. â€”n. Estimate, conjecture.  i guess colloq. I think it likely; i suppose. [origin uncertain]'),
(17738, 'g', '\r\nGuesswork', ' n. Process of or results got by guessing.'),
