(18247, 'h', '\r\nHawk2', ' v. Carry about or offer (goods) for sale. [back-formation from *hawker]'),
(18248, 'h', '\r\nHawk3', ' v. 1 clear the throat noisily. 2 (foll. By up) bring (phlegm etc.) Up from the throat. [imitative]'),
(18249, 'h', '\r\nHawker', ' n. Person who travels about selling goods. [low german or dutch]'),
