(18327, 'h', '\r\nHedge', ' â€”n. 1 fence or boundary of dense bushes or shrubs. 2 protection against possible loss. â€”v. (-ging) 1 surround or bound with a hedge. 2 (foll. By in) enclose. 3 a reduce one''s risk of loss on (a bet or speculation) by compensating transactions on the other side. B avoid committing oneself. [old english]'),
(18328, 'h', '\r\nHedgehog', ' n. Small insect-eating mammal with a piglike snout and a coat of spines, rolling itself up into a ball when attacked.'),
