(18375, 'h', '\r\nHello', ' (also hallo, hullo) â€”int. Expression of informal greeting, or of surprise, or to call attention. â€”n. (pl. -s) cry of â€˜helloâ€™. [var. Of earlier hollo]'),
(18376, 'h', '\r\nHell''s', 'angel  n. Member of a gang of male motor-cycle enthusiasts notorious for outrageous and violent behaviour.'),
(18377, 'h', '\r\nHelm', ' n. Tiller or wheel for controlling a ship''s rudder.  at the helm in control; at the head of an organization etc. [old english]'),
