(18423, 'h', '\r\nHerald', ' â€”n. 1 official messenger bringing news. 2 forerunner, harbinger. 3 a hist. Officer responsible for state ceremonial and etiquette. B official concerned with pedigrees and coats of arms. â€”v. Proclaim the approach of; usher in.  heraldic adj. [french from germanic]'),
