(18632, 'h', '\r\nHinge', ' â€”n. 1 movable joint on which a door, lid, etc., turns or swings. 2 principle on which all depends. â€”v. (-ging) 1 (foll. By on) depend (on a principle, an event, etc.). 2 attach or be attached by a hinge. [related to *hang]'),
