(18654, 'h', '\r\nHire', ' â€”v. (-ring) 1 purchase the temporary use of (a thing) (hired a van). 2 esp. Us employ (a person). â€”n. 1 hiring or being hired. 2 payment for this.  for (or on) hire ready to be hired. Hire out grant the temporary use of (a thing) for payment.  hireable adj. Hirer n. [old english]'),
