(18885, 'h', '\r\nHem2', ' â€”int. Calling attention or expressing hesitation by a slight cough. â€”n. Utterance of this. â€”v. (-mm-) say hem; hesitate in speech.  hem and haw = hum and haw (see *hum). [imitative]'),
(18886, 'h', '\r\nHemal', ' adj. (brit. Haem-) of the blood. [greek haima blood]'),
