(18897, 'h', '\r\nHemophiliac', ' n. (brit. Haem-) person with haemophilia.'),
(18898, 'h', '\r\nHemorrhage', ' (brit. Haem-) â€”n. 1 profuse loss of blood from a ruptured blood-vessel. 2 damaging loss, esp. Of people or assets. â€”v. (-ging) suffer a haemorrhage. [greek haima blood, rhegnumi burst]'),
