(19200, 'h', '\r\nHer', ' â€”pron. 1 objective case of *she (i like her). 2 colloq. She (it''s her all right; am older than her). â€”poss. Pron. (attrib.) Of or belonging to her or herself (her house; her own business). [old english dative and genitive of *she]'),
