(19480, 'h', '\r\nHoarse', ' adj. 1 (of the voice) rough and deep; husky, croaking. 2 having such a voice.  hoarsely adv. Hoarseness n. [old norse]'),
(19481, 'h', '\r\nHoary', ' adj. (-ier, -iest) 1 a (of hair) grey or white with age. B having such hair; aged. 2 old and trite (hoary joke). [old english]'),
(19482, 'h', '\r\nHoax', ' â€”n. Humorous or malicious deception. â€”v. Deceive (a person) with a hoax. [probably a shortening of hocus in *hocus-pocus]'),
