(19484, 'h', '\r\nHobble', ' â€”v. (-ling) 1 walk lamely; limp. 2 tie together the legs of (a horse etc.) To prevent it from straying. â€”n. 1 uneven or infirm gait. 2 rope etc. For hobbling a horse etc. [probably low german]'),
(19485, 'h', '\r\nHobby', ' n. (pl. -ies) leisure-time activity pursued for pleasure. [from the name robin]'),
(19486, 'h', '\r\nHobby-horse', ' n. 1 child''s toy consisting of a stick with a horse''s head. 2 favourite subject or idea.'),
