(20529, 'i', '\r\nIndent', ' â€”v. 1 make or impress marks, notches, dents, etc. In. 2 start (a line of print or writing) further from the margin than others. 3 draw up (a legal document) in duplicate. 4 a (often foll. By on, upon a person, for a thing) make a requisition. B order (goods) by requisition. â€”n. 1 a order (esp. From abroad) for goods. B official requisition for stores. 2 indented line. 3 indentation. 4 indenture. [latin dens dentis tooth]'),
(20530, 'i', '\r\nIndentation', ' n. 1 indenting or being indented. 2 notch.'),
