(20936, 'i', '\r\nInstrumentation', ' n. 1 a provision or use of instruments. B instruments collectively. 2 a arrangement of music for instruments. B the particular instruments used in a piece.'),
(20937, 'i', '\r\nInsubordinate', ' adj. Disobedient; rebellious.  insubordination n.'),
