(21200, 'i', '\r\nInvisible', 'exports  n.pl. (also invisible imports etc.) Intangible commodities, esp. Services, involving payment between countries.'),
(21201, 'i', '\r\nInvitation', ' n. 1 inviting or being invited. 2 letter or card etc. Used to invite.'),
(21202, 'i', '\r\nInvite', ' â€”v. (-ting) 1 (often foll. By to, or to + infin.) Ask (a person) courteously to come, or to do something. 2 make a formal courteous request for. 3 tend to call forth unintentionally. 4 a attract. B be attractive. â€”n. Colloq. Invitation. [latin invito]'),
