(21446, 'j', '\r\nJaywalk', ' v. Cross a road carelessly or dangerously.  jaywalker n.'),
(21447, 'j', '\r\nJazz', ' â€”n. 1 rhythmic syncopated esp. Improvised music of black us origin. 2 slang pretentious talk or behaviour (all that jazz). â€”v. Play or dance to jazz.  jazz up brighten or enliven.  jazzer n. [origin uncertain]'),
