(21479, 'j', '\r\nJeremiah', ' n. Dismal prophet, denouncer of the times. [lamentations of jeremiah, in the old testament]'),
(21480, 'j', '\r\nJerk1', ' â€”n. 1 sharp sudden pull, twist, twitch, start, etc. 2 spasmodic muscular twitch. 3 (in pl.) Colloq. Exercises (physical jerks). 4 slang fool. â€”v. Move, pull, thrust, twist, throw, etc., with a jerk.  jerk off coarse slang masturbate. [imitative]'),
