(21505, 'j', '\r\nJet', 'set  n. Wealthy people who travel widely, esp. For pleasure.  jet-setter n. Jet-setting n. & attrib. Adj.'),
(21506, 'j', '\r\nJettison', ' â€”v. 1 a throw (esp. Heavy material) overboard to lighten a ship etc. B drop (goods) from an aircraft. 2 abandon; get rid of. â€”n. Jettisoning. [anglo-french getteson: related to *jet1]'),
