(21633, 'j', '\r\nJug', ' â€”n. 1 deep vessel for liquids, with a handle and a lip for pouring. 2 contents of this. 3 slang prison. â€”v. (-gg-) (usu. As jugged adj.) Stew or boil (esp. Hare) in a casserole etc.  jugful n. (pl. -s). [origin uncertain]'),
