(21635, 'j', '\r\nJuggle', ' â€”v. (-ling) 1 a (often foll. By with) keep several objects in the air at once by throwing and catching. B perform such feats with (balls etc.). 2 deal with (several activities) at once. 3 (often foll. By with) misrepresent or rearrange (facts) adroitly. â€”n. 1 juggling. 2 fraud.  juggler n. [french from latin jocus jest]'),
(21636, 'j', '\r\nJugoslav', ' var. Of *yugoslav.'),
