(21984, 'k', '\r\nKnotty', ' adj. (-ier, -iest) 1 full of knots. 2 puzzling (knotty problem).'),
(21985, 'k', '\r\nKnow', ' v. (past knew; past part. Known) 1 (often foll. By that, how, what, etc.) A have in the mind; have learnt; be able to recall (knows a lot about cars). B (also absol.) Be aware of (a fact) (i think he knows). C have a good command of (knew german; knows his tables).'),
