(21989, 'k', '\r\nKnowingly', ' adv. 1 consciously; intentionally (wouldn''t knowingly hurt him). 2 in a knowing manner (smiled knowingly).'),
(21990, 'k', '\r\nKnowledge', ' n. 1 a (usu. Foll. By of) awareness or familiarity (of or with a person or thing) (have no knowledge of that). B person''s range of information. 2 a (usu. Foll. By of) understanding of a subject etc. (good knowledge of greek). B sum of what is known (every branch of knowledge).  to my knowledge as far as i know.'),
