(22748, 'l', '\r\nLimb2', ' n. Specified edge of the sun, moon, etc. [latin limbus hem, border]'),
(22749, 'l', '\r\nLimber1', ' â€”adj. 1 lithe. 2 flexible. â€”v. (usu. Foll. By up) 1 make (oneself or a part of the body etc.) Supple. 2 warm up in preparation for athletic etc. Activity. [origin uncertain]'),
(22750, 'l', '\r\nLimber2', ' â€”n. Detachable front part of a gun-carriage. â€”v. Attach a limber to. [perhaps from latin limo -onis shaft]'),
