(23862, 'm', '\r\nMat1', ' â€”n. 1 small piece of coarse material on a floor, esp. For wiping one''s shoes on. 2 piece of cork, rubber, etc., to protect a surface from a hot dish etc. Placed on it. 3 padded floor covering in gymnastics, wrestling, etc. â€”v. (-tt-) (esp. As matted adj.) Entangle or become entangled in a thick mass (matted hair).  on the mat slang being reprimanded. [old english]'),
