(24916, 'm', '\r\nMonsieur', ' n. (pl. Messieurs) title used of or to a french-speaking man, corresponding to mr or sir. [french mon my, sieur lord]'),
(24917, 'm', '\r\nMonsignor', ' n. (pl. -nori) title of various roman catholic priests and officials. [italian: related to *monseigneur]'),
(24918, 'm', '\r\nMonsoon', ' n. 1 wind in s. Asia, esp. In the indian ocean. 2 rainy season accompanying the summer monsoon. [arabic mawsim]'),
(24919, 'm', '\r\nMonster', ' n. 1 imaginary creature, usu. Large and frightening, made up of incongruous elements. 2 inhumanly cruel or wicked person. 3 misshapen animal or plant. 4 large, usu. Ugly, animal or thing. 5 (attrib.) Huge. [latin monstrum from moneo warn]'),
(24920, 'm', '\r\nMonstrance', ' n. Rc ch. Vessel in which the host is exposed for veneration. [latin monstro show]'),
