(25009, 'm', '\r\nMortar', ' â€”n. 1 mixture of lime or cement, sand, and water, for bonding bricks or stones. 2 short large-bore cannon for firing shells at high angles. 3 vessel in which ingredients are pounded with a pestle. â€”v. 1 plaster or join with mortar. 2 bombard with mortar shells. [latin mortarium]'),
