(25011, 'm', '\r\nMortgage', ' â€”n. 1 a conveyance of property to a creditor as security for a debt (usu. One incurred by the purchase of the property). B deed effecting this. 2 sum of money lent by this. â€”v. (-ging) convey (a property) by mortgage.  mortgageable adj. [french, = dead pledge: related to *gage1]'),
(25012, 'm', '\r\nMortgagee', ' n. Creditor in a mortgage.'),
(25013, 'm', '\r\nMortgager', ' n. (also mortgagor) debtor in a mortgage.'),
