(25231, 'm', '\r\nMummy2', ' n. (pl. -ies) body of a human being or animal embalmed for burial, esp. In ancient egypt. [persian mum wax]'),
(25232, 'm', '\r\nMumps', ' n.pl. (treated as sing.) Infectious disease with swelling of the neck and face. [imitative of mouth-shape]'),
(25233, 'm', '\r\nMunch', ' v. Eat steadily with a marked action of the jaws. [imitative]'),
(25234, 'm', '\r\nMundane', ' adj. 1 dull, routine. 2 of this world.  mundanely adv. Mundanity n. [latin mundus world]'),
(25235, 'm', '\r\nMung', ' n. (in full mung bean) leguminous indian plant used as food. [hindi mung]'),
(25236, 'm', '\r\nMunicipal', ' adj. Of a municipality or its self-government.  municipalize v. (also -ise) (-zing or -sing). Municipally adv. [latin municipium free city]'),
