(25892, 'n', '\r\nNoose', ' â€”n. 1 loop with a running knot. 2 snare, bond. â€”v. (-sing) catch with or enclose in a noose. [french no(u)s from latin nodus *node]'),
(25893, 'n', '\r\nNor', ' conj. And not; and not either (neither one thing nor the other; can neither read nor write). [contraction of obsolete nother: related to *no2, *whether]'),
