(26681, 'o', '\r\nOstler', ' n. Hist. Stableman at an inn. [related to *hostel]'),
(26682, 'o', '\r\nOstracize', ' v. (also -ise) (-zing or -sing) exclude from society; refuse to associate with.  ostracism n. [greek (ostrakon potsherd, on which a vote was recorded in ancient athens to expel a powerful or unpopular citizen)]'),
