(26971, 'o', '\r\nOwe', ' v. (owing) 1 a be under obligation (to a person etc.) To pay or repay (money, gratitude, etc.). B (usu. Foll. By for) be in debt. 2 have a duty to render (owe allegiance). 3 (usu. Foll. By to) be indebted to a person or thing for (we owe our success to the weather). [old english]'),
(26972, 'o', '\r\nOwing', ' predic. Adj. 1 owed; yet to be paid. 2 (foll. By to) a caused by. B (as prep.) Because of.'),
(26973, 'o', '\r\nUsage', ' the use of owing to as a preposition meaning â€˜because ofâ€™ is entirely acceptable (e.g. Couldn''t come owing to the snow), unlike this use of due to.'),
