(27043, 'p', '\r\nPact', ' n. Agreement; treaty. [latin pactum]'),
(27044, 'p', '\r\nPad1', ' â€”n. 1 thick piece of soft material used to protect, fill out hollows, hold or absorb liquid, etc. 2 sheets of blank paper fastened together at one edge, for writing or drawing on. 3 fleshy underpart of an animal''s foot or of a human finger. 4 guard for the leg and ankle in sports. 5 flat surface for helicopter take-off or rocket-launching. 6 slang lodgings, flat, etc. 7 floating leaf of a water lily. â€”v. (-dd-) 1 provide with a pad or padding; stuff. 2 (foll. By out) lengthen or fill out (a book etc.) With unnecessary material. [probably low german or dutch]'),
(27045, 'p', '\r\nPad2', ' â€”v. (-dd-) 1 walk with a soft dull steady step. 2 travel, or tramp along (a road etc.), on foot. â€”n. Sound of soft steady steps. [low german pad *path]'),
(27046, 'p', '\r\nPadded', 'cell  n. Room with padded walls in a mental hospital.'),
(27047, 'p', '\r\nPadding', ' n. Soft material used to pad or stuff.'),
