(27079, 'p', '\r\nPail', ' n. 1 bucket. 2 amount contained in this.  pailful n. (pl. -s). [old english]'),
(27080, 'p', '\r\nPain', ' â€”n. 1 any unpleasant bodily sensation produced by illness, accident, etc. 2 mental suffering. 3 (also pain in the neck or arse) colloq. Troublesome person or thing; nuisance. â€”v. 1 cause pain to. 2 (as pained adj.) Expressing pain (pained expression).  be at (or take) pains take great care. In pain suffering pain.'),
