(27789, 'p', '\r\nPerceptive', ' adj. 1 sensitive; discerning. 2 capable of perceiving. perceptively adv. Perceptiveness n. Perceptivity n.'),
(27790, 'p', '\r\nPerch1', ' â€”n. 1 bar, branch, etc. Used by a bird to rest on. 2 high place for a person or thing to rest on. 3  hist. Measure of length, esp. For land, of 51/2 yards. â€”v. (usu. Foll. By on) settle or rest on or as on a perch etc. [latin pertica pole]'),
