(28783, 'p', '\r\nPoppy', 'day  n. = *remembrance sunday.'),
(28784, 'p', '\r\nPopulace', ' n. The common people. [italian: related to *popular]'),
(28785, 'p', '\r\nPopular', ' adj. 1 liked by many people. 2 a of or for the general public. B prevalent among the general public (popular fallacies). 3 (sometimes derog.) Adapted to the understanding, taste, or means of the people (popular science; the popular press).  popularity n. Popularly adv.'),
