(30303, 'r', '\r\nRansom', ' â€”n. 1 money demanded or paid for the release of a prisoner. 2 liberation of a prisoner in return for this. â€”v. 1 buy the freedom or restoration of; redeem. 2 = hold to ransom (see *hold1). 3 release for a ransom. [latin: related to *redemption]'),
(30304, 'r', '\r\nRant', ' â€”v. Speak loudly, bombastically, violently, or theatrically. â€”n. Piece of ranting.  rant and rave express anger noisily and forcefully. [dutch]'),
