(30306, 'r', '\r\nRaoc', ' abbr. Royal army ordnance corps.'),
(30307, 'r', '\r\nRap1', ' â€”n. 1 smart slight blow. 2 knock, sharp tapping sound. 3 slang blame, punishment. 4 a rhythmic monologue recited to music. B (in full rap music) style of rock music with words recited. â€”v. (-pp-) 1 strike smartly. 2 knock; make a sharp tapping sound. 3 criticize adversely. 4 perform a rap.  take the rap suffer the consequences.  rapper n. [probably imitative]'),
(30308, 'r', '\r\nRap2', ' n. Small amount, the least bit (don''t care a rap). [irish ropaire counterfeit coin]'),
(30309, 'r', '\r\nRapacious', ' adj. Grasping, extortionate, predatory.  rapacity n. [latin rapax: related to *rape1]'),
(30310, 'r', '\r\nRape1', ' â€”n. 1 a act of forcing a woman or girl to have sexual intercourse against her will. B forcible sodomy. 2 (often foll. By of) violent assault or plunder, forcible interference. â€”v. (-ping) commit rape on. [latin rapio seize]'),
(30311, 'r', '\r\nRape2', ' n. Plant grown as fodder, and for its seed from which oil is extracted. [latin rapum, rapa turnip]'),
(30312, 'r', '\r\nRapid', ' â€”adj. (-er, -est) 1 quick, swift. 2 acting or completed in a short time. 3 (of a slope) descending steeply. â€”n. (usu. In pl.) Steep descent in a river-bed, with a swift current.  rapidity n. Rapidly adv. Rapidness n.  [latin: related to *rape1]'),
(30313, 'r', '\r\nRapid', 'eye movement  n. Type of jerky movement of the eyes during dreaming.'),
(30314, 'r', '\r\nRapier', ' n. 1 light slender sword for thrusting. 2 (attrib.) Sharp (rapier wit). [french rapiÃ¨re]'),
(30315, 'r', '\r\nRapine', ' n. Rhet. Plundering. [latin: related to *rape1]'),
(30316, 'r', '\r\nRapist', ' n. Person who commits rape.'),
(30317, 'r', '\r\nRapport', ' n. Relationship or communication, esp. When useful and harmonious. [latin porto carry]'),
