(30319, 'r', '\r\nRapscallion', ' n. Archaic or joc. Rascal. [perhaps from *rascal]'),
(30320, 'r', '\r\nRapt', ' adj. 1 fully absorbed or intent, enraptured. 2 carried away with feeling or lofty thought. [latin raptus: related to *rape1]'),
