(31658, 'r', '\r\nRÃ¶ntgen', ' var. Of *roentgen.'),
(31659, 'r', '\r\nRood', ' n. 1 crucifix, esp. One raised on a rood-screen. 2 quarter of an acre. [old english]'),
(31660, 'r', '\r\nRood-screen', ' n. Carved screen separating nave and chancel.'),
(31661, 'r', '\r\nRoof', ' â€”n. (pl. -s) 1 a upper covering of a building. B top of a covered vehicle. C top inner surface of an oven, refrigerator, etc. 2 overhead rock in a cave or mine etc. â€”v. 1 (often foll. By in, over) cover with or as with a roof. 2 be the roof of.  go through the roof colloq. (of prices etc.) Rise dramatically. Hit (or go through) the roof colloq. Become very angry. [old english]'),
