(31986, 's', '\r\nSacrosanct', ' adj. Most sacred; inviolable.  sacrosanctity n. [latin: related to *sacred, *saint]'),
(31987, 's', '\r\nSacrum', ' n. (pl. Sacra or -s) triangular bone between the two hip-bones. [latin os sacrum sacred bone]'),
(31988, 's', '\r\nSad', ' adj. (sadder, saddest) 1 unhappy. 2 causing sorrow. 3 regrettable. 4 shameful, deplorable.  sadden v. Sadly adv. Sadness n. [old english]'),
(31989, 's', '\r\nSaddle', ' â€”n. 1 seat of leather etc. Strapped on a horse etc. For riding. 2 bicycle etc. Seat. 3 joint of meat consisting of the two loins. 4 ridge rising to a summit at each end. â€”v. (-ling) 1 put a saddle on (a horse etc.). 2 (foll. By with) burden (a person) with a task etc.  in the saddle 1 mounted. 2 in office or control. [old english]'),
(31990, 's', '\r\nSaddleback', ' n. 1 roof of a tower with two opposite gables. 2 hill with a concave upper outline. 3 black pig with a white stripe across the back.  saddlebacked adj.'),
