(32017, 's', '\r\nSafety', 'razor  n. Razor with a guard to prevent cutting the skin.'),
(32018, 's', '\r\nSafety-valve', ' n. 1 (in a steam boiler) automatic valve relieving excess pressure. 2 means of venting excitement etc. Harmlessly.'),
(32019, 's', '\r\n', 'saffron  â€”n. 1 deep yellow food colouring and flavouring made from dried crocus stigmas. 2 colour of this. â€”adj. Deep yellow. [french from arabic]'),
(32020, 's', '\r\nSag', ' â€”v. (-gg-) 1 sink or subside, esp. Unevenly. 2 have a downward bulge or curve in the middle. 3 fall in price. â€”n. State or extent of sagging.  saggy adj. [low german or dutch]'),
(32021, 's', '\r\nSaga', ' n. 1 long heroic story, esp. Medieval icelandic or norwegian. 2 series of connected novels concerning a family''s history etc. 3 long involved story. [old norse: related to *saw3]'),
(32022, 's', '\r\nSagacious', ' adj. Showing insight or good judgement.  sagacity n. [latin sagax -acis]'),
(32023, 's', '\r\nSage1', ' n. Culinary herb with dull greyish-green leaves. [french from latin *salvia]'),
(32024, 's', '\r\nSage2', ' â€”n. Often iron. Wise man. â€”adj. Wise, judicious, experienced.  sagely adv. [french from latin sapio be wise]'),
(32025, 's', '\r\nSagebrush', ' n. Growth of shrubby aromatic plants in some semi-arid regions of western n. America.'),
(32026, 's', '\r\nSagittarius', ' n. (pl. -es) 1 constellation and ninth sign of the zodiac (the archer). 2 person born when the sun is in this sign.  sagittarian adj. & n. [latin, = archer]'),
(32027, 's', '\r\nSago', ' n. (pl. -s) 1 a starch used in puddings etc. 2 (in full sago palm) any of several tropical palms and cycads yielding this. [malay]'),
