(32035, 's', '\r\nSailplane', ' n. Glider designed for sustained flight.'),
(32036, 's', '\r\nSainfoin', ' n. Pink-flowered fodder-plant. [latin sanctus holy, foenum hay]'),
(32037, 's', '\r\nSaint', ' â€”n. (abbr. St or s; pl. Sts or ss) 1 holy or (in some churches) formally canonized person regarded as worthy of special veneration. 2 very virtuous person. â€”v. (as sainted adj.) Saintly.  sainthood n. Saintlike adj. [latin sanctus holy]'),
(32038, 's', '\r\nSt', 'bernard  n. (in full st bernard dog) very large dog of a breed orig. Kept in the alps to rescue travellers.'),
(32039, 's', '\r\nSt', 'john''s wort  n. Yellow-flowered plant.'),
(32040, 's', '\r\nSt', 'leger  n. Horse-race at doncaster for three-year-olds. [from the name of the founder]'),
(32041, 's', '\r\nSaintly', ' adj. (-ier, -iest) very holy or virtuous.  saintliness n.'),
(32042, 's', '\r\nSt', 'vitus''s dance  n. Disease producing involuntary convulsive movements of the body.'),
(32043, 's', '\r\nSake1', ' n.  for christ''s (or god''s or goodness'' or heaven''s or pete''s etc.) Sake expression of impatience, supplication, anger, etc. For the sake of (or for one''s sake) out of consideration for; in the interest of; because of; in order to please, honour, get, or keep. [old english]'),
(32044, 's', '\r\nSake2', ' n. Japanese rice wine. [japanese]'),
(32045, 's', '\r\nSalaam', ' â€”n. 1 (chiefly as a muslim greeting) peace! 2 muslim low bow with the right palm on the forehead. 3 (in pl.) Respectful compliments. â€”v. Make a salaam (to). [arabic]'),
(32046, 's', '\r\nSalacious', ' adj. 1 indecently erotic. 2 lecherous.  salaciousness n. Salacity n. [latin salax -acis: related to *salient]'),
(32047, 's', '\r\nSalad', ' n. Cold mixture of usu. Raw vegetables, often with a dressing. [french salade from latin sal salt]'),
(32048, 's', '\r\nSalad', 'cream  n. Creamy salad-dressing.'),
