(32055, 's', '\r\nSale', ' n. 1 exchange of a commodity for money etc.; act or instance of selling. 2 amount sold (sales were enormous). 3 temporary offering of goods at reduced prices. 4 a event at which goods are sold. B public auction.  on (or for) sale offered for purchase. [old english]'),
(32056, 's', '\r\nSaleable', ' adj. Fit or likely to be sold.  saleability n.'),
