(32723, 's', '\r\nSecular', ' adj. 1 not concerned with religion; not sacred; worldly (secular education; secular music). 2 (of clerics) not monastic.  secularism n. Secularize v. (also -ise) (-zing or -sing). Secularization n. [latin saeculum an age]'),
(32724, 's', '\r\nSecure', ' â€”adj. 1 untroubled by danger or fear. 2 safe. 3 reliable; stable; fixed. â€”v. (-ring) 1 make secure or safe. 2 fasten or close securely. 3 succeed in obtaining.  securely adv. [latin se without, cura care]'),
