(32760, 's', '\r\nSeersucker', ' n. Linen, cotton, etc. Fabric with a puckered surface. [persian]'),
(32761, 's', '\r\nSee-saw', ' â€”n. 1 a long plank balanced on a central support, for children to sit on at each end and move up and down alternately. B this game. 2 up-and-down or to-and-fro motion. 3 close contest with alternating advantage. â€”v. 1 play on a see-saw. 2 move up and down. 3 vacillate in policy, emotion, etc. â€”adj. & adv. With up-and-down or backward-and-forward motion. [reduplication of *saw1]'),
