(34256, 's', '\r\nSole1', ' â€”n. 1 undersurface of the foot. 2 part of a shoe, sock, etc., under the foot, esp. Other than the heel. 3 lower surface or base of a plough, golf-club head, etc. â€”v. (-ling) provide (a shoe etc.) With a sole.  -soled adj. (in comb.). [latin solea sandal]'),
(34257, 's', '\r\nSole2', ' n. (pl. Same or -s) flat-fish used as food. [latin solea sandal, which the shape of fish resembles]'),
