(34289, 's', '\r\nSolute', ' n. Dissolved substance.'),
(34290, 's', '\r\nSolution', ' n. 1 solving or means of solving a problem. 2 a conversion of a solid or gas into a liquid by mixture with a liquid. B state resulting from this. 3 dissolving or being dissolved.'),
(34291, 's', '\r\nSolve', ' v. (-ving) answer, remove, or effectively deal with (a problem).  solvable adj.'),
(34292, 's', '\r\nSolvent', ' â€”adj. 1 able to pay one''s debts; not in debt. 2 able to dissolve or form a solution with something. â€”n. Solvent liquid etc.  solvency n. (in sense 2 of adj.).'),
(34293, 's', '\r\nSomatic', ' adj. Of the body, not of the mind.  somatically adv. [greek soma -mat- body]'),
(34294, 's', '\r\nSomber', ' adj. (also brit. Sombre) dark, gloomy, dismal.  sombrely adv. Sombreness n. [latin sub ombra under shade]'),
(34295, 's', '\r\nSombre', ' adj. (also us somber) dark, gloomy, dismal.  sombrely adv. Sombreness n. [latin sub ombra under shade]'),
(34296, 's', '\r\nSombrero', ' n. (pl. -s) broad-brimmed hat worn esp. In latin america. [spanish: related to *sombre]'),
(34297, 's', '\r\nSome', ' â€”adj. 1 unspecified amount or number of (some water; some apples; some of them). 2 unknown or unspecified (some day; some fool broke it). 3 approximately (some ten days). 4 considerable (went to some trouble; at some cost). 5 (usu. Stressed) a at least a modicum of (have some consideration). B such up to a point (that is some help). C colloq.'),
(34298, 's', '\r\n-some1', ' suffix forming adjectives meaning: 1 producing (fearsome). 2 characterized by being (gladsome). 3 apt to (tiresome; meddlesome). 4 suitable for (cuddlesome). [old english]'),
