(35614, 's', '\r\nSuccessful', ' adj. Having success; prosperous.  successfully adv.'),
(35615, 's', '\r\nSuccession', ' n. 1 a process of following in order; succeeding. B series of things or people one after another. 2 a right of succeeding to the throne, an office, inheritance, etc. B act or process of so succeeding. C those having such a right.  in succession one after another. In succession to as the successor of.'),
(35616, 's', '\r\nSuccessive', ' adj. Following one after another; consecutive.  successively adv.'),
