(37881, 't', '\r\nTug', ' â€”v. (-gg-) 1 (often foll. By at) pull hard or violently; jerk. 2 tow (a ship etc.) By a tugboat. â€”n. 1 hard, violent, or jerky pull. 2 sudden strong emotion. 3 small powerful boat for towing ships. [related to *tow1]'),
(37882, 't', '\r\nTugboat', ' n. = *tug n. 3.'),
(37883, 't', '\r\nTug', 'of love  n. Colloq. Dispute over the custody of a child.'),
(37884, 't', '\r\nTug', 'of war  n. 1 trial of strength between two sides pulling opposite ways on a rope. 2 decisive or severe contest.'),
