(37913, 't', '\r\nTuning-fork', ' n. Two-pronged steel fork giving a particular note when struck.'),
(37914, 't', '\r\nTunnel', ' â€”n. 1 underground passage dug through a hill or under a road, river, etc., esp. For a railway or road. 2 underground passage dug by an animal. â€”v. (-ll-; us -l-) 1 (foll. By through, into, etc.) Make a tunnel through. 2 make (one''s way) by tunnelling. [french diminutive of tonne *tun]'),
(37915, 't', '\r\nTunnel', 'vision  n. 1 vision which is poor or lost outside the centre of the normal field of vision. 2 colloq. Inability to grasp a situation''s wider implications.'),
(37916, 't', '\r\nTunny', ' n. (pl. Same or -ies) = *tuna. [greek thunnos]'),
(37917, 't', '\r\nTup', ' â€”n. Ram. â€”v. (-pp-) (of a ram) copulate with (a ewe). [origin unknown]'),
(37918, 't', '\r\nTupi', ' â€”n. (pl. Same or -s) 1 member of an american indian people of the amazon valley. 2 their language. â€”adj. Of this people or language. [tupi]'),
(37919, 't', '\r\nTuppence', ' n. = *twopence. [phonetic spelling]'),
(37920, 't', '\r\nTuppenny', ' adj. = *twopenny. [phonetic spelling]'),
(37921, 't', '\r\nTupperware', ' n. Propr. Range of plastic containers for storing food. [tupper, name of the manufacturer]'),
(37922, 't', '\r\nTurban', ' n. 1 man''s headdress of fabric wound round a cap or the head, worn esp. By muslims and sikhs. 2 woman''s hat resembling this.  turbaned adj. [persian: cf. *tulip]'),
(37923, 't', '\r\nTurbid', ' adj. 1 (of a liquid or colour) muddy, thick; not clear. 2 (of style etc.) Confused, disordered.  turbidity n. [latin turba crowd]'),
(37924, 't', '\r\nUsage', ' turbid is sometimes confused with turgid which means â€˜swollen, inflated; pompousâ€™.'),
(37925, 't', '\r\nTurbine', ' n. Rotary motor driven by a flow of water, steam, gas, wind, etc. [latin turbo -in- spinning-top, whirlwind]'),
(37926, 't', '\r\nTurbo', ' n. (pl. -s) = *turbocharger.'),
