(38175, 'u', '\r\nUn-3', ' prefix chem. Denoting â€˜oneâ€™, combined with other numerical roots nil (= 0), un (= 1), bi (= 2), etc., to form the names of elements based on the atomic number, and terminated with -ium, e.g. Unnilquadium = 104, ununbium = 112.  [latin unus one]'),
