(40549, 'w', '\r\nWing-nut', ' n. Nut with projections for the fingers to turn it.'),
(40550, 'w', '\r\nWing-span', ' n. (also wing-spread) measurement right across the wings.'),
(40551, 'w', '\r\nWink', ' â€”v. 1 (often foll. By at) close and open one eye quickly, esp. As a signal. 2 close and open (one or both eyes) quickly. 3 (of a light etc.) Twinkle; (of an indicator) flash on and off. â€”n. 1 act of winking. 2 colloq. Short sleep.  in a wink very quickly. Wink at purposely avoid seeing; pretend not to notice.  winker n. (in sense 3 of v.). [old english]'),
