(40601, 'w', '\r\nWit', ' n. 1 (in sing. Or pl.) Intelligence; quick understanding. 2 a unexpected combining or contrasting of ideas or expressions. B power of giving pleasure by this. 3 person possessing such power.  at one''s wit''s (or wits'') end utterly at a loss or in despair. Have (or keep) one''s wits about one be alert. Live by one''s wits live by ingenious or crafty expedients, without a settled occupation. Out of one''s wits mad. To wit that is to say, namely. [old english]'),
